  "caption": "Quinn woke up with a small bump on the wrist, named it Gerald, and nearly took the internet's advice to hit it with a book.\n\nA wrist bump like this is often a ganglion: a harmless, fluid-filled lump. Many shrink or disappear over months to years, so watching and waiting is often reasonable. Hitting it can cause injury, and it often comes back anyway.\n\nWhat often helps: go easy on heavy bent-back wrist positions (try fists or handles for push-ups), use a splint briefly if it's achy, keep a neutral wrist when typing, and get a GP check the first time.\n\nGet seen if the lump is hard, fixed or growing, or you have night pain, numbness, weakness or feel unwell.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
